<!--
  sce:std/shared/record_list.scxml — one copy of a shared list of records, a statechart
  of the standard library (docs/adr/0042), written under datamodel="sce-static"
  (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md, "Static data model"). The same document is a person's
  copy and the hub the copies send to; `record_list.join` says which. A statechart that
  keeps a list of its own records invokes it as a child session
  (`<invoke type="scxml" src="sce:std/shared/record_list.scxml">`), turns each command
  into the field writes it sends the list, and keeps its own view from what the list
  tells it (below, "What the list tells its parent"); a host may also run it on its own.

  A record is a row of fields (record_write). The numbers of the rows and of the fields,
  and what each field means, are the application's: the list keeps a number or a text
  for each and reads neither. Each field of each row is a multi-value register: a write
  gives the field one more value, known by the stamp of the write (its dot), and a person
  who writes over a field writes over the values they have SEEN, no others. So two people
  who change the same field of one row at once, neither having seen the other's write,
  both keep theirs, on every copy, whatever order the changes reach it in and however
  many times each does; and a person who writes after seeing them replaces them all. A
  field with one value reads as that value, and with more than one says it was changed
  twice at once, and which values, for a person to choose from.

  The registers are an observed-remove set of the standard `orset_*` algorithms: a
  write is an add of the register's element with the write's dot as its tag, writing
  over a value is a tombstone of the value's tag, and what a field holds is the adds no
  tombstone names. A copy holds exactly those: a tombstone takes the add it names out of
  `adds` as it arrives (orset_live of the add and the tombstone), and an add that a
  tombstone already names is not taken in. So `adds` is the set's value, and a write is
  judged against the tombstones and the adds one pass each, never against every pair.
  The element is `id * 65536 + field`: a row is a uint32 and a field a uint16
  (record_write), so the pair is one uint64 below 2^48 and no two registers share one,
  whatever the numbers; it is below 2^53 as well, which the Interpreter's integers hold
  exactly, so no lane meets a limit another does not. What a set cannot carry is the
  value itself, a number and a text, so each live add has its value in `values`, beside
  it, taken in when the add is live and taken out when a tombstone names it. The standard
  `mv_value_*` algorithms keep them: the machine assigns a write's text into a record of
  its own first (a payload's text is not handed to an algorithm, and that assignment is
  where a text past its bound is refused), and the record is what `mv_value_keep`
  records, bounded as its schema says, and `mv_value_drop` forgets. That is the whole of
  what this document adds to the merge.

  The clock is moved by what a copy sees as well as by what it does: a change made after
  reading someone else's sorts after it.

  A change is a unit (docs/adr/0046). It is the commands a copy is given from the first
  after the last change ended up to the first that does not say `more` (record_edit):
  each command with `more` is held in `staged`, and the one that ends the change closes it
  (`record_list.close`), where the change is judged whole (the copy's member may write,
  no register is written twice, the room, the size), stamped once, and turned into its
  operations: a write-over of every value the copy holds in a register the change names,
  then a write of every register it edits, all at the change's one stamp. A change that
  fails a test is refused whole, with nothing stamped, sent or taken in. An operation is
  taken in by `record_list.take` and sent on by `record_list.pass`, two events with no
  data that each read the next operation of their own queue (`taking`, `passing`), so
  every operation of a change is taken in before any is sent. A change of one operation
  is sent as one write or one supersede, as the first revision of the list sent it; a
  change of more is as many messages, each carrying `parts` (and a write-over the
  change's stamp as `atWallTime` and `atCounter`), and a copy holds such a part in
  `pending` until it holds every part of its change, then takes them in together, so a
  parent is told the change once (`record_list.arrive`). The hub passes each part on as
  it comes. A part already taken in is not held again, and takes the other parts held
  of its change in with it; a resync takes in every part held, and a settle drops those
  of a change at or before its floor.

  A copy that has lost changes for good (restarted from an older save, so that what it
  lacks is something its peers believe delivered, and no retry repairs it) finds them with
  a digest and takes only what it lacks. Each copy keeps a merkle digest of its changes
  (merge/merkle_insert: a trie over the minute of each change's dot, a node the XOR of
  the hashes under it). A change is a live add or a tombstone; an add that a tombstone
  names leaves the digest when the tombstone arrives (XOR again), and the tombstone stays,
  so two copies hold the same digest exactly when they hold the same live adds and
  tombstones, whatever order the changes reached each in. The hash is a 32-bit mix of the
  register, the dot and whether it is an add or a tombstone (merge/merkle_change_hash),
  every part of each taken whole.

  The host raises `record_list.resync` on a copy when its link is back. A message cannot
  carry a list, so the digest is not sent: it is walked, one node to a message
  (`record_list.node`: depth, prefix, hash). A copy that is sent a node compares it with
  its own at that place; where they differ it answers with its own three children of the
  node (a child it holds nothing under is sent with hash 0, so the peer finds what only
  the peer holds), down to the last depth, 30, where a node is one minute: there each side
  sends the changes it holds for that minute as the ordinary `record_list.write` and
  `record_list.supersede` they were, which every copy takes in once whoever sends them and
  however often. merkle_diff is not used for the walk: it compares two whole digests held
  in one place, and here the peer's arrives a node at a time, so the walk is made by the
  messages. The digest's keeping is merkle_insert's.

  The root has three children and each node three, thirty levels down, which is every
  minute a signed 64-bit millisecond clock holds (merkle_node): a change at any wall time
  is on a path the walk takes. A wall time of today is under a run of fourteen nodes that
  hold the whole digest, which the walk passes one level to a message each; that is the
  same for every change however many there are, and a walk for many changes shares it.
  The messages of a walk are the nodes where the copies differ, three to a level, and
  grow with the changes they differ in and not with the time they were made at.

  A tombstone names its register by the element, and the supersede sent for it takes the
  element back to the row and the field (`element / 65536`, `element % 65536`).

  A copy that is written to for long enough has to forget what is settled, and the
  copies decide when they may. The host asks the hub (`record_list.settle`: an instant);
  the hub asks each person's copy what it holds of the changes up to it
  (`record_list.propose`); each person moves its clock past the instant, so that it stamps
  nothing at or before it again, and answers with a hash of its adds and tombstones up to
  it (`record_list.ack`, record_settled). When both answers are the hub's own, every copy
  holds the same up to the instant and none will add to it, whatever order the messages
  came in and however often: the hub tells every copy to forget (`record_list.floor`), and
  each forgets the tombstones it held when it answered. From then on a write stamped at or
  before the floor is not taken in: what a copy does not hold of it, it forgot. A copy
  whose answer was not the hub's, restarted from an old save, is told the floor and finds
  that it never held what the others settled: it forgets nothing and says it is `stale`,
  since the tombstones that would tell it which of its values were written over are gone
  from its peers. `record_list.compact` is the host's own word, for a host that knows.

  A copy keeps every list in a room it is built with (`sce:limit`), and a write that
  would pass it fails half way, which no copy can undo. The host therefore gives a list
  less room than the build holds (`record_list.room`), and a copy refuses a change of its
  own whole when it holds as much as it was given: before it stamps or sends anything,
  counted in `full`. A change is refused for the values when the values it would leave
  pass the room (one that writes no more than it writes over never is), and for the
  tombstones or the digest when the copy holds as many as it was let. What lifts it is a
  settle, which forgets tombstones. A change that is a person's own is the one judged,
  and what a person sent is taken in as it is, so the room is kept below the build's by
  what the people of one list can write at once.

  Every bound of the list is a name a build may give another number (the limit option
  of sce-codegen, docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md, "A bound a deployment chooses"), and a
  build that names none is the list as written: `merge_entries` (1024
  adds, tombstones and the lists a change is judged by), `merge_values` (512 values),
  `merge_digest` (2048 nodes of the digest), `merge_text` (the 96 bytes of text a write
  carries and a value keeps), `shared_typed_text` (the 32 bytes of text a person types,
  record_edit; a build that raises it keeps `merge_text` at least as large),
  `shared_roster` (64 members), `shared_answers` (512 answers to a settle),
  `shared_staged` (32 commands one change stages), `shared_parts` (64 operations of one
  change, and parts of changes not yet whole a copy holds) and `shared_moved` (64
  registers a change moves before they are told, at least `shared_parts`, since a change
  of n operations moves at most n). Each name is carried by the standard algorithms and
  schemas the list reads through, so the machine and what it calls move together. Every
  copy of one list is built with the same numbers.

  What the list tells its parent. A statechart that invokes the list hands it `announce`
  (`<param name="announce" expr="true"/>`), and from then on the list tells it, once for
  each change it takes in, every register that change moved, whatever its source (a
  person's edit, a peer's write or supersede, a resync): `record_list.register`
  (record_register) with the row, the field, how many live values the register holds
  (`count`, 0 when every value was written over) and the first of them in the order of
  their dots (register_values), then `record_list.value` (record_value) for each further
  one, with its place in that order (`ordinal`, from 1). A settle and a compact change no
  value and are not told. An operation that moves a register names it to the list itself
  (`record_list.announce`, record_announce), which keeps the registers named in `moved`
  and, for the first of them, raises `record_list.tell`; every operation of the change is
  already waiting before that, so the telling is made once, after the whole change: a
  person's edit, a write-over of each value it saw and then a write, is told as the one
  register it moved, as it stands after the write, and a change of several fields as
  each of them once. A parent may name a register itself by sending the list
  `record_list.announce`, to be told what it holds.

  A list a host started has no parent, and `#_parent` names no session there: `announce`
  keeps the value its <data> gives it, false, and the list tells no one. The condition is
  what the list keeps of how it was started, and it is read where the telling is made, so
  nothing is sent to `#_parent` by a list no statechart started, whatever asks it to. The
  send names `#_parent` by an expression among the routes it declares (`sce:targets`)
  rather than as a written target: a written `#_parent` makes a machine one that is only
  ever invoked (the C11 backend gives it no entry of its own, and C++ a parent type), and
  this one is started by a host as often as by a parent. `announced` counts the events
  told.

  Its peers. The list sends to its peers by two routes and names no peer of its own:
  `#hub`, by which a person's copy reaches the hub, and `#people`, by which the hub reaches
  every person's copy at once. They are the targets a Mesh deployment binds for the machine
  (`machines.<m>.bindings` of deploy.yaml, SCE_MESH.md "Discovery"): `#hub` to the hub's
  endpoint, `#people` to one topic every person's copy reads, so a list of any number of
  people is one route. Which copy is the hub and what each copy's node is are the host's
  word (`record_list.join`), and nothing of the protocol depends on the number a node is
  given. A hub sends a person's change to `#people` whoever made it, the person included,
  who already holds it and takes nothing from it; a node the hub means for one person
  (`to`) is read by that person and let go by the others. The hub's own change is the
  one it relays: it is taken in here and sent on to `#people` as any change is, and never
  sent to `#hub`, which is the hub itself.

  What a copy does to itself never waits on what it sends (docs/adr/0046). A send to a
  peer the host gave no route to (no Mesh router: a copy on one device, or one whose link
  was never attached) is `error.execution` where it is made, which ends its block. So in
  every transition the copy queues what it does to itself before it sends anything to a
  peer, and a send to a peer is the last act of its block: a copy with no router takes
  every change it makes in, and counts each send it could not make in `refusals`. Its
  first `record_list.resync` on a link shares what it holds.

  `values` and `digest` are what a run compares across copies.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0" initial="open" datamodel="sce-static" name="record_list">
  <!-- Every import names its document by its library name, sibling or not: the list is
       read from the library as `sce:std/shared/record_list.scxml`, and also from a file
       a build stands beside other documents, where a relative name would resolve against
       that file's own directory. -->
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_join.scxml" as="Join"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_edit.scxml" as="Edit"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_write.scxml" as="Write"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_supersede.scxml" as="Supersede"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_keep.scxml" as="Keep"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_node.scxml" as="PeerNode"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_visit.scxml" as="Visit"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_share.scxml" as="Share"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/merkle_node.scxml" as="Node"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_timestamp.scxml" as="Hlc"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/orset_entry.scxml" as="Entry"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value.scxml" as="Value"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_send.scxml" as="HlcSend"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_receive.scxml" as="HlcReceive"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/orset_union.scxml" as="OrsetUnion"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/orset_live.scxml" as="OrsetLive"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_holds.scxml" as="MvValueHolds"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_keep.scxml" as="MvValueKeep"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_drop.scxml" as="MvValueDrop"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/merkle_insert.scxml" as="MerkleInsert"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/merkle_change_hash.scxml" as="MerkleChangeHash"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_compact.scxml" as="Compact"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_settle.scxml" as="Settle"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_propose.scxml" as="Propose"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_ack.scxml" as="Ack"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_floor.scxml" as="Floor"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_answer.scxml" as="Answer"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/shared/record_settled.scxml" as="RecordSettled"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_room.scxml" as="Room"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_role.scxml" as="Role"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_member.scxml" as="Member"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/shared/record_roster.scxml" as="RecordRoster"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_announce.scxml" as="Announce"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/shared/register_values.scxml" as="RegisterValues"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_part.scxml" as="Part"/>
  <datamodel>
    <data id="node" sce:type="uint64" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="hub" sce:type="bool" expr="false" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="clock" sce:type="record:Hlc" sce:direction="out">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="stamp" sce:type="record:Hlc">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- The bounds of the lists a deployment may move are named (`sce:limit`): the
         lists of entries, of values and of the digest are as large as the standard
         algorithms that return them, which carry the same names, so a build that gives
         a name a number moves the machine and the algorithms together. -->
    <data id="adds" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;" sce:capacity="1024" sce:limit="merge_entries" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="tombstones" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;" sce:capacity="1024" sce:limit="merge_entries" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="one" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;" sce:capacity="1024" sce:limit="merge_entries"/>
    <data id="stable" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;" sce:capacity="1024" sce:limit="merge_entries"/>
    <data id="entry" sce:type="record:Entry">
      <sce:set name="element" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="values" sce:type="list&lt;record:Value&gt;" sce:capacity="512" sce:limit="merge_values" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- The text a person types, held to the 32 bytes a person writes (record_edit), the
         bound `shared_typed_text` names: a write has room for more, for what a host puts
         there when it keeps the content from the hub (record_write), and a text past the
         bound that a person typed is refused as one past the room. -->
    <data id="typed" sce:type="string" sce:capacity="32" sce:limit="shared_typed_text" expr="''"/>
    <data id="held" sce:type="record:Value">
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="digest" sce:type="list&lt;record:Node&gt;" sce:capacity="2048" sce:limit="merge_digest" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="mine" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="shareId" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="shareField" sce:type="uint16" expr="0"/>
    <data id="known" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="wasLive" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="isLive" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="present" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="refusals" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- What the copies have settled (record_list.settle): `floor`, the instant up to
         which this copy has forgotten, `stale` when the hub settled an instant this copy
         did not hold the same of, and `late` the writes refused for being stamped at or
         before the floor. `frozenFor` and `frozenHash` are what the copy held of the
         tombstones and the adds up to the instant it was last asked about, kept in
         `stable`; the hub keeps the round it has open (`pending`, -1 for none) and what
         each person answered. -->
    <data id="floor" sce:type="int64" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="stale" sce:type="bool" expr="false" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="late" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="frozenFor" sce:type="int64" expr="-1"/>
    <data id="frozenHash" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="pending" sce:type="int64" expr="-1"/>
    <data id="members" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="agreeing" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="answers" sce:type="list&lt;record:Answer&gt;" sce:capacity="512" sce:limit="shared_answers"/>
    <data id="answer" sce:type="record:Answer">
      <sce:set name="sender" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="hash" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="agreed" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <!-- How much the host lets this copy hold (record_list.room), 0 for no limit, and
         the changes a person made that were refused for it (`full`). -->
    <data id="roomValues" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="roomHistory" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="roomDigest" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="full" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- What the host lets each member do (record_list.role), the changes that were
         refused for it (`denied`) and what the change in hand is judged by: whether its
         author may write. -->
    <data id="roster" sce:type="list&lt;record:Member&gt;" sce:capacity="64" sce:limit="shared_roster"/>
    <data id="denied" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="forbidden" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="authorized" sce:type="bool" expr="true"/>
    <!-- What the list tells the statechart that invoked it: `announce`, handed by the
         <invoke> that starts the list and false for a list a host started, which tells
         no one; `announced`, the events told; and what the telling in hand reads, the
         live values of one register in the order of their dots and the place of each. -->
    <data id="announce" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="announced" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- The registers the change in hand moved, by their element, kept until the change
         is told, and whether the one named now is among them already. -->
    <data id="moved" sce:type="list&lt;uint64&gt;" sce:capacity="64" sce:limit="shared_moved"/>
    <data id="listed" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="live" sce:type="list&lt;record:Value&gt;" sce:capacity="512" sce:limit="merge_values"/>
    <data id="ordinal" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <!-- What a register that holds no value is told as: the number 0, no text and the
         dot of no write, each of its field's own type. -->
    <data id="empty" sce:type="record:Value">
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- A change (docs/adr/0046): the commands of the change in hand (`staged`), whether
         the command in hand says the change goes on (`holding`), the `now` of the one that
         ends it, whether the change is refused (`spoiled`), and whether the statement in
         hand is one whose failure refuses it (`probing`): a text past its bound and a
         list past its room fail as an assignment does, ending the block, and
         error.execution is where the change is then refused. What a change is judged by:
         the values it writes over (`gone`), the registers it writes (`writes`), and
         whether the value in hand is in a register it names (`covered`). -->
    <data id="staged" sce:type="list&lt;record:Part&gt;" sce:capacity="32" sce:limit="shared_staged"/>
    <data id="holding" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="closingNow" sce:type="int64" expr="0"/>
    <data id="spoiled" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="probing" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="gone" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="writes" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="covered" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <!-- The operations to take in (`taking`, the next at `took`) and to send on
         (`passing`, the next at `passed`), each read by an event of its own that carries
         no data; the parts of changes not yet whole (`waiting`), and a list the parts
         kept are gathered in while the others are taken out (`kept`); the part in hand,
         a peer's operation as it arrived (`part`), and the operation in hand (`op`); and
         what a part is judged by: whether the copy holds it already (`already`) and how
         many parts of its change the copy holds (`count`). -->
    <data id="taking" sce:type="list&lt;record:Part&gt;" sce:capacity="64" sce:limit="shared_parts"/>
    <data id="took" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="passing" sce:type="list&lt;record:Part&gt;" sce:capacity="64" sce:limit="shared_parts"/>
    <data id="passed" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="waiting" sce:type="list&lt;record:Part&gt;" sce:capacity="64" sce:limit="shared_parts"/>
    <data id="kept" sce:type="list&lt;record:Part&gt;" sce:capacity="64" sce:limit="shared_parts"/>
    <data id="part" sce:type="record:Part">
      <sce:set name="kind" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="by" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="atWallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="atCounter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="parts" expr="1"/>
    </data>
    <data id="op" sce:type="record:Part">
      <sce:set name="kind" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="by" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="atWallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="atCounter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="parts" expr="1"/>
    </data>
    <data id="already" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="count" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
  </datamodel>
  <state id="open">
    <transition event="record_list.join" type="internal">
      <assign location="node" expr="_event.data.node"/>
      <assign location="hub" expr="_event.data.hub"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- What the host lets this copy hold (record_list.room): the most values,
         tombstones and digest nodes. 0 is no limit of that kind. -->
    <transition event="record_list.room" type="internal">
      <assign location="roomValues" expr="_event.data.values"/>
      <assign location="roomHistory" expr="_event.data.history"/>
      <assign location="roomDigest" expr="_event.data.digest"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- What the host lets a member do (record_list.role): the member takes the role, or
         is taken off the roster by a role of 0. A copy with no roster refuses no one, and
         one with a roster refuses a change of its own member's that is not a writer's,
         and the hub what a member that is not a writer sends it. The roster is the host's
         word and the copies take it alike, as they take the room. -->
    <transition event="record_list.role" type="internal">
      <assign location="roster" expr="RecordRoster(roster, _event.data.node, _event.data.role)"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- A person's edit of one field: a command of a change (docs/adr/0046). It is
         staged, and the command that does not say `more` ends the change, which
         `record_list.close` judges, stamps and takes in whole. The text is read first,
         into a place nothing else reads: a text past what a person writes is an
         assignment that fails and ends the block, and error.execution refuses the
         change, as a change past the room of `staged` is. Nothing is stamped or sent
         here. A change already refused stages nothing more, and is ended all the same. -->
    <transition event="record_list.edit" type="internal">
      <assign location="holding" expr="_event.data.more"/>
      <if cond="!spoiled">
        <assign location="probing" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="typed" expr="_event.data.text"/>
        <assign location="part.kind" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="part.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="part.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="part.value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
        <assign location="part.text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
        <sce:append target="staged" expr="part"/>
        <assign location="probing" expr="false"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!holding">
        <assign location="closingNow" expr="_event.data.now"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.close"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The change in hand is ended: judged whole, and taken in, or refused whole.

         It is refused when the copy's member may not write (record_list.role: with no
         roster set, anyone may; with one, a member whose role is a writer's), counted in
         `denied`; when two of its commands write or clear one register, since the order
         of a change's commands means nothing; and when it would pass the room the host
         gave the copy (record_list.room), counted in `full`: the values it would leave
         past `values` (a change that writes no more values than it writes over adds
         none), or the copy holds as many tombstones or digest nodes as it was let, since
         each change adds to them and what lets it through is a settle. A change that
         names nothing the copy holds and writes nothing is no change.

         A change that passes is stamped once, with the `now` of the command that ended
         it, and turned into its operations in `taking`: a write-over of each value the
         copy holds in a register the change names, in the order of `adds`, then a write of
         each register it edits, in the order of its commands, every one at the change's
         stamp and carrying how many there are. A change of more operations than
         `taking` holds is refused whole, by error.execution, before the clock moves. Then
         every operation is queued to be taken in here, and after them every one to be
         sent on: the copy holds the change before it sends any of it. -->
    <transition event="record_list.close" type="internal">
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="forbidden" expr="true"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === node &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="forbidden" expr="false"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="forbidden">
          <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
          <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
        </if>
      </if>
      <if cond="!spoiled">
        <foreach array="staged" item="earlier" index="earlierAt">
          <foreach array="staged" item="later" index="laterAt">
            <if cond="laterAt &gt; earlierAt &amp;&amp; earlier.kind !== 2 &amp;&amp; later.kind !== 2 &amp;&amp; earlier.id === later.id &amp;&amp; earlier.field === later.field">
              <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <assign location="gone" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="writes" expr="0"/>
      <if cond="!spoiled">
        <foreach array="adds" item="a">
          <assign location="covered" expr="false"/>
          <foreach array="staged" item="s">
            <if cond="a.element / 65536 === s.id &amp;&amp; (s.kind === 2 || a.element % 65536 === s.field)">
              <assign location="covered" expr="true"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <if cond="covered">
            <assign location="gone" expr="gone + 1"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <foreach array="staged" item="s">
          <if cond="s.kind === 0">
            <assign location="writes" expr="writes + 1"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; gone + writes &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; ((roomValues &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; writes &gt; gone &amp;&amp; len(values) + writes &gt; roomValues + gone) || (roomHistory &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; len(tombstones) &gt;= roomHistory) || (roomDigest &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; len(digest) &gt;= roomDigest))">
        <assign location="full" expr="full + 1"/>
        <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; gone + writes &gt; 0">
        <assign location="probing" expr="true"/>
        <assign location="stamp" expr="HlcSend(clock, closingNow, node)"/>
        <sce:clear target="taking"/>
        <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="adds" item="a">
          <assign location="covered" expr="false"/>
          <foreach array="staged" item="s">
            <if cond="a.element / 65536 === s.id &amp;&amp; (s.kind === 2 || a.element % 65536 === s.field)">
              <assign location="covered" expr="true"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <if cond="covered">
            <assign location="part.kind" expr="1"/>
            <assign location="part.id" expr="a.element / 65536"/>
            <assign location="part.field" expr="a.element % 65536"/>
            <assign location="part.value" expr="0"/>
            <assign location="part.text" expr="''"/>
            <assign location="part.wallTime" expr="a.wallTime"/>
            <assign location="part.counter" expr="a.counter"/>
            <assign location="part.nodeId" expr="a.nodeId"/>
            <assign location="part.by" expr="node"/>
            <assign location="part.atWallTime" expr="stamp.wallTime"/>
            <assign location="part.atCounter" expr="stamp.counter"/>
            <assign location="part.parts" expr="gone + writes"/>
            <sce:append target="taking" expr="part"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <foreach array="staged" item="s">
          <if cond="s.kind === 0">
            <assign location="part.kind" expr="0"/>
            <assign location="part.id" expr="s.id"/>
            <assign location="part.field" expr="s.field"/>
            <assign location="part.value" expr="s.value"/>
            <assign location="part.text" expr="s.text"/>
            <assign location="part.wallTime" expr="stamp.wallTime"/>
            <assign location="part.counter" expr="stamp.counter"/>
            <assign location="part.nodeId" expr="node"/>
            <assign location="part.by" expr="node"/>
            <assign location="part.atWallTime" expr="stamp.wallTime"/>
            <assign location="part.atCounter" expr="stamp.counter"/>
            <assign location="part.parts" expr="gone + writes"/>
            <sce:append target="taking" expr="part"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <assign location="probing" expr="false"/>
        <sce:clear target="staged"/>
        <assign location="clock" expr="stamp"/>
        <sce:clear target="passing"/>
        <assign location="passed" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="taking" item="t">
          <sce:append target="passing" expr="t"/>
        </foreach>
        <foreach array="taking" item="t">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.take"/>
        </foreach>
        <foreach array="passing" item="t">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.pass"/>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!spoiled &amp;&amp; gone + writes === 0">
        <sce:clear target="staged"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="spoiled">
        <sce:clear target="staged"/>
        <assign location="spoiled" expr="false"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The next operation of `taking`, taken in: a write gives its register one more
         value, once, and a write-over takes the value it names out. This is where every
         operation is merged, a copy's own and a peer's alike. -->
    <transition event="record_list.take" type="internal">
      <assign location="op" expr="taking[took]"/>
      <assign location="took" expr="took + 1"/>
      <!-- A write: one more value, once. The text is read into the value it is kept in.
           A peer's write moves the clock up to it; a write this copy made and no longer
           holds, which a peer sends back when the copy has been restarted from an older
           save, is taken in with the clock moved up to it, so that what the copy writes
           next is stamped after it and never with a dot it has already used. A write made
           here that the clock already stands at (every one, as it is first taken in)
           moves nothing. Whether the write is live: no tombstone names it. One a person
           wrote over before it arrived is not taken in, and only a live one is added. And
           whether its value is already held, which a write that arrives twice is. A
           write that gives the register a value it did not hold is told to the parent
           (record_list.announce). -->
      <if cond="op.kind === 0">
        <assign location="held.text" expr="op.text"/>
        <if cond="op.nodeId !== node">
          <assign location="stamp.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="stamp.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <assign location="stamp.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          <assign location="clock" expr="HlcReceive(clock, stamp, clock.wallTime, node)"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="op.nodeId === node &amp;&amp; (op.wallTime &gt; clock.wallTime || (op.wallTime === clock.wallTime &amp;&amp; op.counter &gt; clock.counter))">
          <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="clock.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="op.id"/>
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + op.field"/>
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="isLive" expr="true"/>
        <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
          <if cond="t.element === entry.element &amp;&amp; t.wallTime === entry.wallTime &amp;&amp; t.counter === entry.counter &amp;&amp; t.nodeId === entry.nodeId">
            <assign location="isLive" expr="false"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="isLive">
          <sce:clear target="one"/>
          <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
          <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetUnion(adds, one)"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="held.id" expr="op.id"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="op.field"/>
        <assign location="held.value" expr="op.value"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="present" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="isLive &amp;&amp; !present">
          <assign location="values" expr="MvValueKeep(values, held)"/>
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.keep">
            <param name="kind" expr="0"/>
            <param name="element" expr="entry.element"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="isLive &amp;&amp; !present &amp;&amp; announce">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.announce">
            <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
      <!-- A write-over: the add it names is named by a tombstone, and its value, if
           held, is taken out. A peer's write-over that is part of a change carries the
           change's stamp, which moves the clock up to it as a write does. Whether the
           tombstone is new, which one that arrives twice is not; the add it names is no
           longer live and leaves `adds` (a tombstone that is not new leaves nothing to
           take out); and whether the write it names is held, which is when its add leaves
           the digest as the tombstone enters it. A value taken out is told to the parent
           (record_list.announce). -->
      <if cond="op.kind === 1">
        <if cond="op.atWallTime &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; op.by !== node">
          <assign location="stamp.wallTime" expr="op.atWallTime"/>
          <assign location="stamp.counter" expr="op.atCounter"/>
          <assign location="stamp.nodeId" expr="op.by"/>
          <assign location="clock" expr="HlcReceive(clock, stamp, clock.wallTime, node)"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="op.id"/>
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + op.field"/>
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="known" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
          <if cond="t.element === entry.element &amp;&amp; t.wallTime === entry.wallTime &amp;&amp; t.counter === entry.counter &amp;&amp; t.nodeId === entry.nodeId">
            <assign location="known" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <sce:clear target="one"/>
        <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
        <assign location="tombstones" expr="OrsetUnion(tombstones, one)"/>
        <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetLive(adds, one)"/>
        <assign location="held.id" expr="op.id"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="op.field"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="wasLive" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
        <assign location="values" expr="MvValueDrop(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="!known">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.keep">
            <param name="kind" expr="1"/>
            <param name="element" expr="entry.element"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="wasLive">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.keep">
            <param name="kind" expr="0"/>
            <param name="element" expr="entry.element"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="wasLive &amp;&amp; announce">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.announce">
            <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The next operation of `passing`, sent on: a person's copy sends to the hub, and
         the hub to every person's copy, its own changes and what it relays alike. An
         operation of a change of one is sent as the first revision of the list sent it;
         one of a change of more carries how many parts the change has, and a write-over
         the change's stamp (a write is stamped with it already). The send is the whole of
         the block, so one that fails where it is made fails alone. -->
    <transition event="record_list.pass" type="internal">
      <assign location="op" expr="passing[passed]"/>
      <assign location="passed" expr="passed + 1"/>
      <if cond="op.kind === 0 &amp;&amp; op.parts &lt;= 1 &amp;&amp; !hub">
        <send target="#hub" event="record_list.write">
          <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          <param name="value" expr="op.value"/>
          <param name="text" expr="op.text"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <if cond="op.kind === 0 &amp;&amp; op.parts &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; !hub">
        <send target="#hub" event="record_list.write">
          <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          <param name="value" expr="op.value"/>
          <param name="text" expr="op.text"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          <param name="parts" expr="op.parts"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <if cond="op.kind === 0 &amp;&amp; op.parts &lt;= 1 &amp;&amp; hub">
        <send target="#people" event="record_list.write">
          <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          <param name="value" expr="op.value"/>
          <param name="text" expr="op.text"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <if cond="op.kind === 0 &amp;&amp; op.parts &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; hub">
        <send target="#people" event="record_list.write">
          <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          <param name="value" expr="op.value"/>
          <param name="text" expr="op.text"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          <param name="parts" expr="op.parts"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <if cond="op.kind === 1 &amp;&amp; op.parts &lt;= 1 &amp;&amp; !hub">
        <send target="#hub" event="record_list.supersede">
          <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          <param name="by" expr="op.by"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <if cond="op.kind === 1 &amp;&amp; op.parts &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; !hub">
        <send target="#hub" event="record_list.supersede">
          <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          <param name="by" expr="op.by"/>
          <param name="parts" expr="op.parts"/>
          <param name="atWallTime" expr="op.atWallTime"/>
          <param name="atCounter" expr="op.atCounter"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <if cond="op.kind === 1 &amp;&amp; op.parts &lt;= 1 &amp;&amp; hub">
        <send target="#people" event="record_list.supersede">
          <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          <param name="by" expr="op.by"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <if cond="op.kind === 1 &amp;&amp; op.parts &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; hub">
        <send target="#people" event="record_list.supersede">
          <param name="id" expr="op.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="op.field"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="op.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
          <param name="by" expr="op.by"/>
          <param name="parts" expr="op.parts"/>
          <param name="atWallTime" expr="op.atWallTime"/>
          <param name="atCounter" expr="op.atCounter"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A write stamped at or before the floor is not taken in, from anyone and however
         often it arrives. Everything up to the floor was settled when the copies agreed on
         it: a write of that time that this copy does not hold is one it forgot, with the
         tombstone that named it, and taking it in again would bring the value back. A
         person's copy stamps nothing at or before an instant it has answered for, so no
         write that is new is refused here. -->
    <transition event="record_list.write" cond="floor &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; _event.data.wallTime &lt;= floor" type="internal">
      <!-- It is counted only when this copy does not hold it: a live write that a peer
           shows again, which a repair of another copy sends to every copy that reads the
           same name, is held and changes nothing. -->
      <assign location="held.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
      <assign location="held.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
      <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
      <assign location="held.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
      <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
      <assign location="present" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
      <if cond="!present">
        <assign location="late" expr="late + 1"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A write a peer sent (or the host gave): judged here, and handed on to
         `record_list.arrive` as the part in hand. The hub takes it only from a member the
         host let write (record_list.role): a write whose author is not on a roster that
         is set, or is on it with less than a writer's role, is dropped whole and counted
         in `denied`, as a change a person's copy was not let make is. One whose text does
         not fit changes nothing here and is passed on to no one, rather than being merged
         in part. The change a write is part of is known by its own dot, which is the
         change's stamp. -->
    <transition event="record_list.write" type="internal">
      <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="authorized" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === _event.data.nodeId &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!authorized">
        <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="authorized">
        <assign location="part.text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
        <assign location="part.kind" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="part.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="part.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="part.value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
        <assign location="part.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="part.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="part.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="part.by" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="part.atWallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="part.atCounter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="part.parts" expr="_event.data.parts"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.arrive"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A write-over that is part of a change stamped at or before the floor is let go,
         and counted in `late`, as a write of that time is: every copy held the same up to
         the floor when it was settled, and what this copy does not hold of it, it forgot.
         A write-over that is a change of its own carries no stamp, and is taken as it
         always was. -->
    <transition event="record_list.supersede" cond="floor &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; _event.data.parts &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; _event.data.atWallTime &lt;= floor" type="internal">
      <assign location="late" expr="late + 1"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- A value someone wrote over, as a peer sent it (or the host gave it): judged here
         and handed on to `record_list.arrive` as the part in hand. The hub takes it only
         from a member the host let write, as it takes a write (`by` is who wrote over). -->
    <transition event="record_list.supersede" type="internal">
      <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="authorized" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === _event.data.by &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!authorized">
        <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="authorized">
        <assign location="part.kind" expr="1"/>
        <assign location="part.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="part.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="part.value" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="part.text" expr="''"/>
        <assign location="part.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="part.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="part.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="part.by" expr="_event.data.by"/>
        <assign location="part.atWallTime" expr="_event.data.atWallTime"/>
        <assign location="part.atCounter" expr="_event.data.atCounter"/>
        <assign location="part.parts" expr="_event.data.parts"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.arrive"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The part in hand, as a peer sent it. One that is a change of its own is taken
         in. One of a change of more parts is held in `waiting` until the copy holds every
         part of its change, and then all of them are taken in together, so the change is
         merged, and told, as one: unless the copy holds it already (a write it holds or a
         tombstone names, a tombstone it has), which is not held again; and then every part
         the copy holds of the same change is taken in at once, since the change has
         reached it in pieces already. A part already waiting is not held twice. Last, the
         hub passes it on to every person's copy as it came, its author's included, which
         holds it already and takes nothing from it: the hub holds nothing back from the
         people while a part of a change is late. -->
    <transition event="record_list.arrive" type="internal">
      <if cond="part.parts &gt; 1">
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="part.id"/>
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + part.field"/>
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="part.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="part.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="part.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="already" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
          <if cond="t.element === entry.element &amp;&amp; t.wallTime === entry.wallTime &amp;&amp; t.counter === entry.counter &amp;&amp; t.nodeId === entry.nodeId">
            <assign location="already" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="part.kind === 0">
          <assign location="held.id" expr="part.id"/>
          <assign location="held.field" expr="part.field"/>
          <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="part.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="held.counter" expr="part.counter"/>
          <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="part.nodeId"/>
          <assign location="present" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
          <if cond="present">
            <assign location="already" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </if>
        <assign location="listed" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="waiting" item="w">
          <if cond="w.kind === part.kind &amp;&amp; w.id === part.id &amp;&amp; w.field === part.field &amp;&amp; w.wallTime === part.wallTime &amp;&amp; w.counter === part.counter &amp;&amp; w.nodeId === part.nodeId">
            <assign location="listed" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="!already &amp;&amp; !listed">
          <sce:append target="waiting" expr="part"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="count" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="waiting" item="w">
          <if cond="w.atWallTime === part.atWallTime &amp;&amp; w.atCounter === part.atCounter &amp;&amp; w.by === part.by">
            <assign location="count" expr="count + 1"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="already || count &gt;= part.parts">
          <sce:clear target="taking"/>
          <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
          <sce:clear target="kept"/>
          <foreach array="waiting" item="w">
            <if cond="w.atWallTime === part.atWallTime &amp;&amp; w.atCounter === part.atCounter &amp;&amp; w.by === part.by">
              <sce:append target="taking" expr="w"/>
            </if>
            <if cond="w.atWallTime !== part.atWallTime || w.atCounter !== part.atCounter || w.by !== part.by">
              <sce:append target="kept" expr="w"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <sce:clear target="waiting"/>
          <foreach array="kept" item="k">
            <sce:append target="waiting" expr="k"/>
          </foreach>
          <foreach array="taking" item="t">
            <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.take"/>
          </foreach>
        </if>
      </if>
      <if cond="part.parts &lt;= 1">
        <sce:clear target="taking"/>
        <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
        <sce:append target="taking" expr="part"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.take"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="hub">
        <sce:clear target="passing"/>
        <assign location="passed" expr="0"/>
        <sce:append target="passing" expr="part"/>
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.pass"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A register the change in hand moved, named to be told: kept in `moved` once,
         and for the first one named `record_list.tell` is raised, which waits behind
         every event the change has raised already and so is taken when the change is
         whole. Taken only when a parent started the list asking for it (`announce`): a
         list a host started keeps nothing to tell, whatever raised this. -->
    <transition event="record_list.announce" cond="announce" type="internal">
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="_event.data.id"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + _event.data.field"/>
      <assign location="listed" expr="false"/>
      <foreach array="moved" item="named">
        <if cond="named === entry.element">
          <assign location="listed" expr="true"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="len(moved) === 0">
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.tell"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!listed">
        <sce:append target="moved" expr="entry.element"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- What each register the change moved holds, told to the statechart that invoked
         the list: the first of its live values in the order of their dots with how many
         there are, then each further one with its place, or a count of 0 and the empty
         value when it holds none. `#_parent` is named among the routes the send declares
         and not written as its target, so the machine keeps the entry a host starts it
         by. -->
    <transition event="record_list.tell" cond="announce" type="internal">
      <foreach array="moved" item="named">
        <assign location="shareId" expr="named / 65536"/>
        <assign location="shareField" expr="named % 65536"/>
        <assign location="live" expr="RegisterValues(values, shareId, shareField)"/>
        <if cond="len(live) === 0">
          <send event="record_list.register" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
            <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
            <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
            <param name="count" expr="0"/>
            <param name="value" expr="empty.value"/>
            <param name="text" expr="empty.text"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="empty.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="empty.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="empty.nodeId"/>
          </send>
          <assign location="announced" expr="announced + 1"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="ordinal" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="live" item="r">
          <if cond="ordinal === 0">
            <send event="record_list.register" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="count" expr="len(live)"/>
              <param name="value" expr="r.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="r.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="r.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="r.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="r.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <if cond="ordinal !== 0">
            <send event="record_list.value" targetexpr="'#_parent'" sce:targets="#_parent">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="ordinal" expr="ordinal"/>
              <param name="value" expr="r.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="r.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="r.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="r.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="r.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <assign location="announced" expr="announced + 1"/>
          <assign location="ordinal" expr="ordinal + 1"/>
        </foreach>
      </foreach>
      <sce:clear target="moved"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- A change taken in for the first time, told to the digest: its hash is XORed
         into every node on the path of its minute. An add that a tombstone has named
         is told again, which takes it out. The hash is merkle_change_hash's, of the
         entry the change names and its kind. -->
    <transition event="record_list.keep" type="internal">
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="_event.data.element"/>
      <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
      <assign location="entry.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
      <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
      <assign location="mine" expr="MerkleChangeHash(entry, _event.data.kind)"/>
      <assign location="digest" expr="MerkleInsert(digest, _event.data.wallTime / 60000, mine)"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host's word that the changes up to an instant are settled everywhere: the
         tombstones stamped at or before it go, and leave the digest as they entered it
         (the same hash, XORed again), so that the digest is still the digest of what the
         copy holds, and a copy that is told the same instant holds the same. The adds
         they named left `adds` when each tombstone arrived, and a register's values are
         what no tombstone names, so neither is moved: the tombstones are what grows
         without it, and this is what lets a copy that is written to for years hold only
         what is current (orset_live, the difference that is how a set forgets). -->
    <transition event="record_list.compact" type="internal">
      <sce:clear target="stable"/>
      <assign location="frozenFor" expr="-1"/>
      <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
        <if cond="t.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
          <sce:append target="stable" expr="t"/>
          <assign location="mine" expr="MerkleChangeHash(t, 1)"/>
          <assign location="digest" expr="MerkleInsert(digest, t.wallTime / 60000, mine)"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <assign location="tombstones" expr="OrsetLive(tombstones, stable)"/>
      <if cond="_event.data.before &gt; floor">
        <assign location="floor" expr="_event.data.before"/>
      </if>
      <!-- A part the copy holds of a change stamped at or before the instant is dropped:
           what is settled the copy holds whole already, or it is a copy the host will
           start again. -->
      <sce:clear target="kept"/>
      <foreach array="waiting" item="w">
        <if cond="w.atWallTime &gt; _event.data.before">
          <sce:append target="kept" expr="w"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <sce:clear target="waiting"/>
      <foreach array="kept" item="k">
        <sce:append target="waiting" expr="k"/>
      </foreach>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host asks the hub to settle what is stamped at or before an instant, so that
         the copies decide the instant themselves and no host has to know that every copy
         holds everything up to it. The hub moves its clock past the instant, asks each
         person's copy what it holds (record_list.propose), and repeats the last instant it
         settled to both, so that a copy that missed it is told again. -->
    <transition event="record_list.settle" type="internal">
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.before &gt; floor">
        <assign location="pending" expr="_event.data.before"/>
        <assign location="members" expr="_event.data.members"/>
        <sce:clear target="answers"/>
        <if cond="clock.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
          <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.before + 1"/>
          <assign location="clock.counter" expr="0"/>
        </if>
        <send target="#people" event="record_list.propose">
          <param name="before" expr="_event.data.before"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A person's copy is asked what it holds up to an instant. It moves its clock past
         the instant first, so that what it stamps from now on is after it, and then
         takes what it holds of the tombstones up to the instant and the hash of the
         adds and tombstones (record_settled): the tombstones are what it will forget if
         the hub settles, and no others, so that a tombstone that arrives after it
         answered is kept with the value it names. -->
    <transition event="record_list.propose" type="internal">
      <if cond="!hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.before &gt; floor">
        <if cond="clock.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
          <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.before + 1"/>
          <assign location="clock.counter" expr="0"/>
        </if>
        <sce:clear target="stable"/>
        <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
          <if cond="t.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
            <sce:append target="stable" expr="t"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <assign location="frozenFor" expr="_event.data.before"/>
        <assign location="frozenHash" expr="RecordSettled(adds, tombstones, _event.data.before)"/>
        <send target="#hub" event="record_list.ack">
          <param name="sender" expr="node"/>
          <param name="before" expr="_event.data.before"/>
          <param name="hash" expr="frozenHash"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The hub reads an answer only for the round it has open, and keeps each distinct
         answer (a copy and the hash it gave). A copy whose answer is the hub's own,
         now, held exactly what the hub holds when it answered, and stamps nothing at or
         before the instant after: when as many different copies as the host named
         (`members`) have such an answer, every copy held the same up to the instant, and
         the instant is settled. The hub tells every copy, itself included, to forget. An
         answer that differs settles nothing; the round stays open for a later answer, or
         for the host's next record_list.settle. -->
    <transition event="record_list.ack" type="internal">
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.before === pending">
        <assign location="mine" expr="RecordSettled(adds, tombstones, pending)"/>
        <assign location="known" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="answers" item="a">
          <if cond="a.sender === _event.data.sender &amp;&amp; a.hash === _event.data.hash">
            <assign location="known" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="!known">
          <assign location="answer.sender" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
          <assign location="answer.hash" expr="_event.data.hash"/>
          <sce:append target="answers" expr="answer"/>
        </if>
        <!-- No copy has two answers of one hash, so the answers that are the hub's are
             as many as the copies that hold what it holds. -->
        <assign location="agreeing" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="answers" item="a">
          <if cond="a.hash === mine">
            <assign location="agreeing" expr="agreeing + 1"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="members &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; agreeing &gt;= members">
          <sce:clear target="stable"/>
          <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
            <if cond="t.wallTime &lt;= pending">
              <sce:append target="stable" expr="t"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <assign location="frozenFor" expr="pending"/>
          <assign location="frozenHash" expr="mine"/>
          <!-- The hub's own floor first, and the round closed, then the people told:
               a hub that cannot reach them still settles itself. The instant told is
               `frozenFor`, which holds it until the hub's own floor is taken. -->
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.floor">
            <param name="before" expr="pending"/>
            <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          </send>
          <assign location="pending" expr="-1"/>
          <send target="#people" event="record_list.floor">
            <param name="before" expr="frozenFor"/>
            <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <!-- The copies are told the last instant settled when an answer is not the hub's
             and there was one: a copy that took part in it finds that it holds what was
             agreed or has forgotten it already, and one that did not (restarted from an
             old save) finds that it never did, and is stale. -->
        <if cond="_event.data.hash !== mine &amp;&amp; floor &gt; 0">
          <send target="#people" event="record_list.floor">
            <param name="before" expr="floor"/>
            <param name="hash" expr="agreed"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The hub's word that an instant is settled. A copy that held what the hub says
         every copy held (it answered, or it holds it now) forgets the tombstones it held
         up to the instant, and stamps nothing at or before the instant from here on. A
         copy that holds another thing is not one the hub asked: it forgets nothing, and
         says it is stale, for the host to start it again from what its peers hold, since
         the tombstones its peers forgot are the ones that would tell it which of its
         values were written over. -->
    <transition event="record_list.floor" type="internal">
      <if cond="_event.data.before &gt; floor">
        <if cond="frozenFor !== _event.data.before">
          <sce:clear target="stable"/>
          <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
            <if cond="t.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
              <sce:append target="stable" expr="t"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <assign location="frozenFor" expr="_event.data.before"/>
          <assign location="frozenHash" expr="RecordSettled(adds, tombstones, _event.data.before)"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="frozenHash === _event.data.hash">
          <if cond="clock.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
            <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.before + 1"/>
            <assign location="clock.counter" expr="0"/>
          </if>
          <foreach array="stable" item="t">
            <assign location="mine" expr="MerkleChangeHash(t, 1)"/>
            <assign location="digest" expr="MerkleInsert(digest, t.wallTime / 60000, mine)"/>
          </foreach>
          <assign location="tombstones" expr="OrsetLive(tombstones, stable)"/>
          <assign location="floor" expr="_event.data.before"/>
          <assign location="agreed" expr="_event.data.hash"/>
          <assign location="stale" expr="false"/>
          <assign location="frozenFor" expr="-1"/>
          <!-- A part it holds of a change stamped at or before the instant is dropped:
               every copy held the same up to it, so the copy holds that change already. -->
          <sce:clear target="kept"/>
          <foreach array="waiting" item="w">
            <if cond="w.atWallTime &gt; _event.data.before">
              <sce:append target="kept" expr="w"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <sce:clear target="waiting"/>
          <foreach array="kept" item="k">
            <sce:append target="waiting" expr="k"/>
          </foreach>
        </if>
        <if cond="frozenHash !== _event.data.hash">
          <assign location="stale" expr="true"/>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host's word that this copy's link is back: it takes in every part it holds of
         a change not yet whole, each alone, since what a link lost of them the walk
         gives back one operation at a time, and it shows its peers the root of its
         digest. A person's copy has only the hub to show it to; the hub shows every
         person (to 0), however many the host has. -->
    <transition event="record_list.resync" type="internal">
      <sce:clear target="taking"/>
      <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
      <foreach array="waiting" item="w">
        <sce:append target="taking" expr="w"/>
      </foreach>
      <sce:clear target="waiting"/>
      <foreach array="taking" item="t">
        <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.take"/>
      </foreach>
      <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.visit">
        <param name="to" expr="0"/>
        <param name="depth" expr="0"/>
        <param name="prefix" expr="0"/>
        <param name="reply" expr="false"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <!-- Show a peer the node of this copy's digest at a place: the hash it holds there,
         0 where it holds nothing. -->
    <transition event="record_list.visit" type="internal">
      <assign location="mine" expr="0"/>
      <foreach array="digest" item="n">
        <if cond="n.depth === _event.data.depth &amp;&amp; n.prefix === _event.data.prefix">
          <assign location="mine" expr="n.hash"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="!hub">
        <send target="#hub" event="record_list.node">
          <param name="sender" expr="node"/>
          <param name="to" expr="0"/>
          <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth"/>
          <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
          <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          <param name="reply" expr="_event.data.reply"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <!-- The hub reaches its people by one route, `#people`, which every person's copy
           reads. The node says whom it is for (`to`, 0 for all) and a person that it is
           not for lets it go. -->
      <if cond="hub">
        <send target="#people" event="record_list.node">
          <param name="sender" expr="node"/>
          <param name="to" expr="_event.data.to"/>
          <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth"/>
          <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
          <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          <param name="reply" expr="_event.data.reply"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A node of a peer's digest: where this copy's own differs, the peer is shown the
         children of it, and at a minute the changes of that minute are sent. A node that
         is the same on both sides ends the walk there. At a minute the peer is also shown
         this copy's node once, so that it sends its changes too; that one is marked, and
         is not answered. -->
    <transition event="record_list.node" type="internal">
      <if cond="hub || _event.data.to === 0 || _event.data.to === node">
        <assign location="mine" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="digest" item="n">
          <if cond="n.depth === _event.data.depth &amp;&amp; n.prefix === _event.data.prefix">
            <assign location="mine" expr="n.hash"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="mine !== _event.data.hash &amp;&amp; _event.data.depth &lt; 30">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.visit">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth + 1"/>
            <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix * 3"/>
            <param name="reply" expr="false"/>
          </send>
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.visit">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth + 1"/>
            <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix * 3 + 1"/>
            <param name="reply" expr="false"/>
          </send>
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.visit">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth + 1"/>
            <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix * 3 + 2"/>
            <param name="reply" expr="false"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="mine !== _event.data.hash &amp;&amp; _event.data.depth === 30">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.share">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="minute" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="mine !== _event.data.hash &amp;&amp; _event.data.depth === 30 &amp;&amp; !_event.data.reply">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.visit">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="depth" expr="30"/>
            <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
            <param name="reply" expr="true"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The changes this copy holds that fall in one minute, sent to a peer as the
         writes and supersedes they were. A live write is held with its value; a
         tombstone names its register by the element, which is taken back to the row and
         the field. -->
    <transition event="record_list.share" type="internal">
      <foreach array="values" item="v">
        <if cond="v.wallTime / 60000 === _event.data.minute">
          <assign location="shareId" expr="v.id"/>
          <assign location="shareField" expr="v.field"/>
          <if cond="!hub">
            <send target="#hub" event="record_list.write">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="value" expr="v.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="v.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="v.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="v.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="v.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <if cond="hub">
            <send target="#people" event="record_list.write">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="value" expr="v.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="v.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="v.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="v.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="v.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
        <if cond="t.wallTime / 60000 === _event.data.minute">
          <assign location="shareId" expr="t.element / 65536"/>
          <assign location="shareField" expr="t.element % 65536"/>
          <if cond="!hub">
            <send target="#hub" event="record_list.supersede">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="t.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="t.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="t.nodeId"/>
              <param name="by" expr="node"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <if cond="hub">
            <send target="#people" event="record_list.supersede">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="t.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="t.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="t.nodeId"/>
              <param name="by" expr="node"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </if>
      </foreach>
    </transition>

    <!-- Every failure is counted. One a command or the end of a change met while it was
         staging the change or turning it into its operations (`probing`) refuses the
         change: a text past what a person writes, a change past the room of `staged` or
         of `taking`. The block it stood in has ended, so a command that ended the change
         has its end raised here, where the change is refused whole. -->
    <transition event="error.execution" type="internal">
      <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
      <if cond="probing">
        <assign location="probing" expr="false"/>
        <assign location="spoiled" expr="true"/>
        <if cond="!holding">
          <send target="#_internal" event="record_list.close"/>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>
  </state>
</scxml>
